OPEN_QUESTION InitAsksForBuiltInOrCustomRoles
	QUESTION "does brigade init, or an installer if one comes, ask whether to use the built-in"
		+ "roles or the user's own, and write the answer into config.toml?"
	STATUS open
	RATIONALE "the user ruled on 2026-10-06 that brigade defines default roles and that a user who"
		+ "wants their own configures them, and left open whether an installer asks"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-06 in the refinement of B43"

OPEN_QUESTION WallTimeBudgetOfAClientThatCountsNoSteps
	QUESTION "when a client reports no step count, how does the step budget of a procedure become"
		+ "the wall-time limit of its run?"
	STATUS closed
	RATIONALE "the Blueprint, plan section 17, holds the budget on wall time without a conversion,"
		+ "and only a recipe declares a duration, max_wall; the user left the conversion to a"
		+ "sourced study, measured runs and the documentation of the clients, in the refinement of"
		+ "@TASK.B06"
		REF @TASK.B06
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-06 in the refinement of B06"

OPEN_QUESTION HowBrigadeJoinsAProjectWhoseCorpusAlreadyExists
	QUESTION "when a project registered with brigade already holds an awawa corpus whose schema"
		+ "declares no WAVE, or a TASK with other fields than those brigade reads and writes, does"
		+ "brigade share that corpus, checking its schema, or keep a corpus of its own in a folder"
		+ "of its own?"
	STATUS closed
	RATIONALE "project add registers an existing corpus where it finds it, CORPUS being the common"
		+ "parent of every tracked .awawa file (brigade/registry/discover_project.py), by DESC 3 of"
		+ "@DECISION.TheCorpusFolderIsDeclaredByTheProjectAndDefaultsToCorpus; nothing checks that"
		+ "its schema declares what brigade writes there, the TASK and WAVE entities of @TASK.B10,"
		+ "and --init-corpus of @TASK.B55 says nothing of a folder that already holds a corpus"
		REF @DECISION.TheCorpusFolderIsDeclaredByTheProjectAndDefaultsToCorpus
		REF @TASK.B10
		REF @TASK.B55
	RATIONALE "the options seen in the refinement of B81: a shared corpus, project add checking"
		+ "that the schema declares the types and fields brigade needs and naming the missing ones;"
		+ "or a separate corpus in a folder of brigade's, read as a workspace of its own, two"
		+ "corpora in one repository making the common parent of their files the repository root,"
		+ "which mixes them in one awawa workspace"
	SOURCE "the user's question of 2026-10-09 in the refinement of B81, \"si un corpus préexiste"
		+ "lors de l'installation de brigade il se passe quoi?\", and the answer chosen, an open"
		+ "question blocking B55"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-12 in the refinement of B10, recorded by"
		+ "@DECISION.AProjectChoosesHowBrigadeUsesItsCorpus"
		REF @DECISION.AProjectChoosesHowBrigadeUsesItsCorpus

