OPEN_QUESTION TheKeyOfAWaveInTheLedger
	QUESTION "what keys a wave in the ledger: the name of its REQUEST, <project>_<n>, or the pair"
		+ "project and MILESTONE?"
	STATUS closed
	BLOCKS @TASK.B165
	RATIONALE "today wave.started and task.state are keyed by the MILESTONE name alone,"
		+ "brigade/waves/start_wave.py:34, brigade/commands/tick.py:68,"
		+ "brigade/waves/read_task_states.py:7-12, brigade/tick/build_snapshot.py:130 and"
		+ "brigade/ledger/describe_wave.py:56-57: two projects whose waves name a milestone M1"
		+ "share their task states, and a milestone cannot be relaunched,"
		+ "brigade/planning/record_plan.py:131 refusing the existing integration branch"
	RATIONALE "the candidates: the name of the REQUEST, unique by construction, SPEC 1 of"
		+ "@TASK.B11; the pair project and MILESTONE; neither creates a WAVE type, which"
		+ "@DECISION.AWaveIsAMilestoneOfTheProjectCorpusAndItsBranchIsNamedAfterIt rejects"
		REF @TASK.B11
		REF @DECISION.AWaveIsAMilestoneOfTheProjectCorpusAndItsBranchIsNamedAfterIt
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-17 in the triage of the use-case map, answer \"Open"
		+ "question\""
	SOURCE "use-case map of 2026-10-16, findings X2 and C2"

